    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "The star performer of the Visayas grid, Kepco SPC Power's Unit 2, took a dramatic bow and tripped offline, leaving the grid's designated parent to sound the grand alarm. The supporting cast of other generators had already left the stage, and with high seasonal demand playing the villain, the serious grown-ups orchestrated the big blackout ballet, creating a spectacular power void for millions in the heat-struck region.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Jester",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "result-0"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.88
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "In the grand stage of the power circus, the red-alert maestros faced a predictable crunch ignored, as a mechanical failure by the tripped performer left a significant capacity shortfall. The directive-givers declared a code red and forced a juggling act with people's power, all while the silent ensemble cast of generators remained stubbornly unavailable.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Jester",
        "fragments": [
          "why-1",
          "how-0",
          "how-1",
          "result-0"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.75
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "The weather played the villain, driving energy demand spike into the Visayas grid region, just as the grid's dramatic diva decided on a grand exit. This unscripted dropout forced the panicked puppet-masters to order load shedding, resulting in a record-breaking blackout and highlighting a chronic lack of backup across the energy infrastructure.",
